You can use Jackson library to convert object to DTO. Jackson is a popular library for JSON serialization and deserialization in Java.
Here is an example of how to use Jackson to convert object to DTO:
```
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper;

public class User {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    // getters and setters
}

public class UserDTO {
    private String name;
    private int age;

    // getters and setters
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        User user = new User();
        user.setName("John");
        user.setAge(30);

        ObjectMapper mapper = new ObjectMapper();
        UserDTO userDTO = mapper.convertValue(user, UserDTO.class);

        System.out.println(userDTO.getName()); // prints "John"
        System.out.println(userDTO.getAge()); // prints 30
    }
}
```
In this example, we create an instance of `User` and set its properties. Then we use `ObjectMapper` to convert the `User` object to a `UserDTO` object. The `convertValue` method takes the source object and the target class as arguments and returns the converted object.

You can also use `ObjectMapper` to convert a JSON string to a DTO object:
```
String json = "{\"name\":\"John\",\"age\":30}";
UserDTO userDTO = mapper.readValue(json, UserDTO.class);
```
